[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2877812283","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106239#issuecomment-2877812283","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106239","id":2877812283,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rh-47","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T20:06:09Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T22:16:48Z","body":"Seems a regression between 4.4 dev 2 and 4,4 dev 3, bisecting.\n\nEdit: After two bisects that i was unable to find a culprit i did a test compiling 4.4 dev 2 with MSVC and i found that any build compiled with MSVC shows this bug. I tried to compile with MinGW but the build fails close to the end. \n\nConsidering that using the official build (compiled with MinGW) of 4.4 dev 2 don't reproduce this bug and MSVC shows a different behavior i would do a wild guess that is somehow related with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/92911 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/74830","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2877812283/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2880548723","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106239#issuecomment-2880548723","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106239","id":2880548723,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rsa9z","user":{"login":"snowflower","id":1240280,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNDAyODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1240280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower","html_url":"https://github.com/snowflower","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowflower/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-14T14:52:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-14T14:52:53Z","body":"I can also reproduce this by going to the FileSystem panel and duplicate any existing .gdshader file.\nDuplicate a shader, give the duplicate a unique name, and then tab away from the editor to another application, like a web browser for a short time.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d1a09460-3494-438b-8ecb-8e1a72079092)\nWhen you tab back to the godot editor, you will get the same popup in the initial bug report.\n\nIf you select 'Cancel' the editor the popup will disappear,  but if you tab away to another application and return to the editor, you will get the popup **again**. If you tab away after canceling, then tab back, you can be stuck in this ui loop forever by continuing to press cancel :)\n\nThis popup should really be explaining to the user what file its referring to, it is a bit unnerving to be giving the option to save/reload/cancel *what* file??\nIf I trigger this bug by duplicating any shader in the project, even one that isnt focused in the shader editor, theres no feedback about what shader file its referring to.\nI can reliably reproduce this duplicating any shader from the FileSystem explorer, so the reference to 'this' isnt relevant because its not the shader opened and focused in the shader editor.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/78d93d5e-33c0-45ad-802f-e6bfc44c51ed)\nthe only way to get rid of this popup is to pick 'Resave' which feels like the safer option than 'reload', still this bug makes me nervous when I encounter it myself since 'cancel' doesn't really work.\n\ntested and reproducible on : \nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 9 3950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2880548723/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885319050","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106239#issuecomment-2885319050","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106239","id":2885319050,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6r-nmK","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T00:12:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T00:12:30Z","body":"@Zylann and @snowflower, could you check if this bug is reproducible on Godot 4.4 dev 2 or Godot 4.3 stable?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885319050/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5270192488","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106239#issuecomment-5270192488","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106239","id":5270192488,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOiDBaA","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-12T17:30:05Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T17:56:19Z","body":"I can reproduce this on 4.8. For me, it only happens if the file is opened in the shader editor, and after saving then refocusing the editor. It also seems to only happen once per session, unless the shader file is closed and reopened again.\n\n**EDIT:** Also happens with normal GDShaders.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5270192488/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5450956793","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106239#issuecomment-5450956793","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106239","id":5450956793,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABROb_-Q","user":{"login":"aguneyaltun","id":47734769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzM0NzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47734769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun","html_url":"https://github.com/aguneyaltun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aguneyaltun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T09:40:07Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T09:40:07Z","body":"Since there were no platform tags I tested it on Linux and couldn't reproduce the issue.\n\nSystem: Arch Linux, Sway (Wayland), Vulkan 1.4.354, Forward+, Intel Graphics (MTL).\n\nTested it both for v4.4.1.stable.official and 4.8.\n\nSteps followed as described: created a new ShaderInclude from the inspector (tab shows [*]), clicked out to another window, clicked back on Godot. No dialog appears.\n\nI checked that the focus change is actually registered by the editor, so the refocus code path is being hit and it doesn't produce the dialog here.\n\nHaven't tested X11, so I can only speak for Wayland. Given it's the same commit, this looks Windows-specific. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5450956793/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]